## Why this is vendored rather than installed

FlowAgent is not published to npm, so there is no `npx` form. The upstream distribution is a
Claude Code plugin, and a plugin's cache path is CLI-specific and is wiped on update. The repo is
the source of truth for this project, and an MCP server the repo depends on should not live only
in a cache. So the bundle is committed and `.mcp.json` points at a relative path.

## What it is

A single self-contained ESM bundle — 50+ tools, stdio transport, all dependencies inlined
(MSAL included). Needs Node 18+ and nothing else installed. It shells out to `az` for tokens:

- `https://service.flow.microsoft.com` — flow management (the main path)
- `https://api.powerplatform.com` — connection management, via an inlined MSAL public client

It does **not** require the `pac` CLI. `pac` is used by the *other* plugins in that marketplace
for solution and ALM work, and is not installed on this machine.

## Updating

```bash
git clone --depth 1 --filter=blob:none --sparse \
  https://github.com/microsoft/power-platform-skills.git /tmp/pps
cd /tmp/pps && git sparse-checkout set plugins/power-automate/server
cp plugins/power-automate/server/mcp.mjs <repo>/vendor/flowagent/mcp.mjs
git rev-parse HEAD          # → new pin
sha256sum <repo>/vendor/flowagent/mcp.mjs
```

Then update the pin, size and hash above, restart the MCP server, and re-run a read-only tool
call before trusting it. Do not update mid-engagement without a reason — a silent breaking change
before 8 September 2026 is the risk this pin exists to prevent.

Note: `raw.githubusercontent.com` rate-limits (429) on this bundle. The sparse clone above is the
reliable route.

